  "title": "AI’s next phase is about control as much as capability",
  "summary": "This week’s AI stories point in three directions at once. OpenAI’s reported move away from live internet access underlines the value of controlled training inputs; the Anthropic lawsuit shows that data provenance remains a legal risk; and a fileAI–AWS banking collaboration reflects the pressure to turn models into governed workflows. Taken together, the pattern is less a single breakthrough than an industry learning to trade openness and speed for auditability, permissions and predictable deployment.",
